i don't know if maybe there's a contest  going on between republican senators  who can appear to be the most  disconnected from the modern world  and how we talk about things in 2021 but  if such a contest  exists i would nominate republican  senator  john kennedy no relation to the  democratic  kennedy family in the last month i  brought you the story of senator john  kennedy  strangely trying to equate guns and cars  as well as kind of equating the  regulation of guns and cars you can  check out that segment  from the march 24th show if it sounds  interesting and it is actually pretty  interesting  but yesterday john kennedy was on fox  news ostensibly talking  about i guess police shootings and  police brutality  and he started talking about how we  quote higher  whites blacks and browns  it was as strange a segment as it sounds  let's take a look  there's no justice we can't have a  society without order  and we have decided to hire law  enforcement officials to maintain order  we hire whites blacks browns  men women to maintain  order many many of our of our  law enforcement agencies are are  majority monarch  if you want to sound like a racist  southerner like if you really want to  play the prototypical caricature  of a racist american right-wing  southerner  you say exactly what he said in exactly  that  accent exactly how he talks about whites  blacks and browns that's how you make  yourself look like  the typical uh caricature of a southern  racist american in another moment  from the same appearance senator kennedy  apparently in an effort to push back  against the defund the police movement  which is supported by  very few people he says if you don't  like police next time call a crackhead  that's his word not mine i'll put it  this way if you hate cops just because  they're cops you don't know anything  about them  then next time you get in trouble call a  crackhead  now having said that  what we're really talking about here  what we're talking about here is the  relationship  between crime and race  let's just cut to the chase it is a  statistical fact  that just as it is the case that more  men  than women commit crimes just as it is a  statistical fact  that more younger people than older  people commit crimes  we have racial minorities and ethnic  groups in america that have higher crime  rates  we have to why poverty  but that doesn't tell you anything that  is a sitting  united states senator if you can believe  it this  opens up the possibility of so many  skits and satire on saturday night live  that they must be thanking the comedy  gods right now  if you don't like police call a  crackhead  next time you're in trouble why not just  improve policing  and then feel better about calling the  police most people don't want to  actually defund or abolish the police  why do you need to go to what we have  or crack heads it's a very strange  kind of backwards reverse  rationalization  the choices are police we don't believe  are as well trained as they should be  and drug addicts like how are those the  parameters that we should be selecting  between  and by the way when i was preparing this  segment  i got a phone call and the clip kept  playing without sound  if you want to see a really a scary  movie so to speak  watch senator uh john kennedy speaking  without the audio on it's really the  stuff of nightmares but that's an aside  now there's like one percent  that john kennedy gets correct here  don't hate police for  being police most police officers  are people who are choosing to be police  officers  for admirable good reasons and who never  have complaints  against them about use of force it would  be bad  it would be a non-thinking reason  to hate an individual officer because  they are  a police officer at the same time and  this is where you know it's almost like  they can't hold  two ideas simultaneously at the same  time  you can understand that all  officers can be part of a system  that is not productively serving  a large portion of the people in their  respective communities and that  there are changes there that need to be  made none of it involves  crackheads none of it involves drug  addicts  of any kind now i know that the  caricature is  the left just wants to end police or  defund the police or cancel police or  whatever there are some who want to do  that  most don't but we have the public uh  polling data  on it what most people want is to reform  and restructure the police and i know  that there are some on the left  including in my audience who get mad and  they say  reform has never worked why would it  work now well we've not actually done it  and there are police unions that get in  the way of certain reform  elements that are often recommended and  suggested including a national bad  actors database  that police departments be mandated to  both report to the bad actors database  as well as  um uh to use it for  reference when hiring a new police  officer  i have multiple segments with 10 or 12  possible specific reforms  most people just want to improve  policing there are situations  where you don't need an armed officer to  show up there are situations that are  better de-escalated  by social workers and others but we  could also give police officers better  training as social workers that's  another great idea  better equip them for de-escalation in  many countries police are much better  trained  for de-escalation none of it requires  crack heads and none of it requires  defunding or canceling the police

